[{"id": "R025", "text": "The speaker tests both instruments against the bench and listens to their responses while two explanations conflict. They press the older instrument harder, find the key remains loose, and leave the conclusion that the older instrument causes the break unresolved."}, {"id": "R026", "text": "The speaker rotates and compares two pieces, noting that one edge catches and then releases. They hold the smaller piece against a cloth, leave the other untouched, and treat the observed difference as less significant than the disagreement between explanations."}, {"id": "R027", "text": "The speaker keeps both explanations visible, marks the instrument as unclear, and writes the same assessment on the other side of the paper. They prioritize the edge case and retain the second explanation until the end."}, {"id": "R028", "text": "The speaker separates two pieces, records their difference beside the failure, and identifies the second piece while keeping the first in a pocket. They leave the explanation behind and write the instrument name beside the failure."}, {"id": "R029", "text": "The speaker compares two explanations, notes a small difference, and considers pocketing both pieces but delays doing so. They test the smaller piece with a rusted bolt, leave it at the failure site, and keep the conclusion unchanged while awaiting further observation."}, {"id": "R030", "text": "The speaker folds paper with both instruments, changes the folding method when the paper's shape changes, and sets one explanation aside because both say the same thing. They continue folding until one explanation fits their hand."}, {"id": "R031", "text": "The speaker marks the mismatched contact with grease, runs a short test using a fresh stick, and leaves the older explanation beside the bench. They keep the scratched edge and mismatched stick nearby and observe where the contact catches."}, {"id": "R032", "text": "The speaker follows a sequence of checks involving small amounts, a slow watch, a line, a square, and a date, while keeping the work orderly. They record a small mark, test it, recheck the watch, and aim to keep the process simple."}, {"id": "R033", "text": "The speaker moves two pieces slowly, retains the one set aside, and records the difference on a loose sketchbook page. They keep the other piece in a pocket and wait for it to stop moving."}, {"id": "R034", "text": "The speaker holds the explanations apart, traces an edge, and identifies a faint scratch that resembles a small screw. They leave the older explanation beside the instrument and observe the key's movement when tapped once."}, {"id": "R035", "text": "The speaker records a small amount on a test sheet, checks the explanation, apologizes to the instrument, and leaves it untouched. They photograph the fault, write a verdict, keep the explanations separate, and leave the relevant one in place."}, {"id": "R036", "text": "The speaker notices the gap widening, touches the wrench to their thigh, and stops. They state that one explanation is correct despite the other disagreeing, then lean closer and stop again."}]
